# One line-ending convention for every platform.
#
# The repository stores LF, and a Windows checkout does not rewrite it, so
# `prettier --check` (endOfLine: "lf") means the same thing on Linux, on macOS and
# on Windows. Without this file, a Windows checkout would convert every text file
# and the format check would fail for a contributor who changed nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never line-ending-normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
